# #54 word-match-repair prospective correctness-batch review

**Verdict: PASS for the exact four-role correctness batch, gated in order and stopped at the first non-PASS role.** This is launch approval only; no commands ran in this review.

The candidate is `b29d4c812daf9c4c17591da24b844df31e1d1a71c6e1641dd39e36bf6ab30a14`, with an exact two-hunk patch `3b88b0178cdf7760e1c88e5b906228ba6cdf606c8d97a88ad70038bba8e825ed` relative to `a28692cd…`. The source-bound predecessor diagnostic identifies `check-schedules:kind_value`, `U32`, and the null `Word32` field layout before the `val_arm` failure. The repair reconstructs only a local virtual Word32 match spine from the actual U32/F32 constructor field and ordered Word constructors. It keeps Bool-head and Word31-tail order, derives the 32 match words, and leaves ordinary child layouts and function-boundary `val_to(lay_of(...))` behavior in place. The diff does not alter `INLINE_LAYOUT_LIMIT`, `WIDE`, physical layout/CIDs, budgets, caches, app sources, or installed compiler.

The focused controls cover U32 literal selectors, wildcard/captured values, high-bit and maximum values, head/tail and partial-spine paths, plus finite representable F32 literals/captures and a low-bit-true case. Literal selectors return strings to keep them on the match path. The 369-byte expectation is source-derived, records no runtime inputs, and uses IEEE-754 binary32 bits for the F32 word cases; `F32.to_nat`'s numeric-conversion cases are also reflected. The app oracle remains the independent 224,204-byte source-derived oracle.

Freeze `e6e442deb6814a5c8ac96e31cc785f265401069125274d1d9f3f9acf9d70a577` and launch manifest `8fca16eb751437ed97a54676774918aebb6bbdc66596aa82427e89b12a084d36` bind full JS → full Native → controls JS → controls Native. The four exact plan hashes are `5195f44d…`, `e85aa641…`, `3ddd13a8…`, and `2e1e4c1d…`. All plans retain the existing collector, 112 pins, six resource roots, CPU 3, 30/120/5-second caps, and fresh output targets. Rehashing found no missing or mismatched pins/source files; the expected stdout files match their recorded sizes and hashes. The controls' stock source-check receipt and candidate syntax receipt are successful. No outer lock or new process layer is added.

Approval is limited to these finite correctness checks. It establishes no universal compiler refinement, performance improvement, installed-compiler adoption, or issue closure.
